#: ../../source/docs/qstabilize-mode.rst:5
#: 4d9712af24e54c1e96e90ffddcb01a0e
msgid "QSTABILIZE Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qstabilize-mode.rst:7
#: 490a8597b77f417db028566922f8e74f
msgid "QSTABILIZE mode allows you to fly your vehicle manually, but self-levels the roll and pitch axis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qstabilize-mode.rst:12
#: 4636ae793e1f42e48acd47a97c4fc141
msgid "If you're learning to fly, try :ref:`QHOVER <qhover-mode>` or :ref:`QLOITER <qloiter-mode>` instead of QSTABILIZE. You'll have fewer crashes if you don't need to concentrate on too many controls at once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qstabilize-mode.rst:20
#: c973be374b0248e986039b6b7807b729
msgid "While QSTABILIZE mode does not necessarily require GPS, switching to QRTL or RTL in case of emergency does. Make sure you do have a reliable position estimate prior to arming, most commonly provided by 3D GPS fix with sufficient HDOP. This is required by default in the arming checks. It is highly recommended that these checks not be  disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qstabilize-mode.rst:25
#: 75158d07e7884d6c897e95488e7be99a
msgid "Flying QuadPlane backwards at speed or backwards into high wind is not recommended, since the Plane control surfaces will act backwards and could increase instability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qstabilize-mode.rst:29
#: 689bb79ddc8740cf8db43b3b30bae6c5
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qstabilize-mode.rst:31
#: 241925c03551434d91b596abfe6ad990
msgid "Pilot's roll and pitch input control the lean angle of the QuadPlane. When the pilot releases the roll and pitch sticks the vehicle automatically levels itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qstabilize-mode.rst:34
#: aa21bd0d42104b808944186eaaae4179
msgid "Pilot will need to regularly input roll and pitch commands to keep the vehicle in place as it is pushed around by the wind."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qstabilize-mode.rst:36
#: f63d298639e4480ab3f0a9faf81d6870
msgid "Pilot's yaw input controls the rate of change of the heading.  When the pilot releases the yaw stick the vehicle will maintain its current heading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qstabilize-mode.rst:39
#: 7fd3b2bd49f34d5d900c3d74c753d14d
msgid "Pilot's throttle input controls the average motor speed meaning that constant adjustment of the throttle is required to maintain altitude.  If the pilot puts the throttle completely down the motors will go to their minimum rate (Q_M_SPIN_ARMED) and if the vehicle is flying it will lose attitude control and tumble."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qstabilize-mode.rst:44
#: 788a0b89d502419f9011c77c8fdb7783
msgid "The throttle sent to the motors is automatically adjusted based on the tilt angle of the vehicle (i.e. increased as the vehicle tilts over more) to reduce the compensation the pilot must do as the vehicle's attitude changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qstabilize-mode.rst:51
#: 26d20eed4db7499eaf5f4eba53396b9d
msgid "Always switch into a manual mode such as QSTABILIZE if the autopilot fails to control the vehicle. Maintaining control of your copter is your responsibility."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qstabilize-mode.rst:58
#: 2cdd45c4aa164f27869ce393712d25c5
msgid "Common Problems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qstabilize-mode.rst:60
#: 98e93c40e1294a2cae707c0a55e6db15
msgid "QuadPlane flips immediately upon take-off.  This is usually caused by the motor order being incorrect or spinning in the wrong direction or using an incorrect propeller (clockwise vs counter-clockwise). Check the rc connections for your autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qstabilize-mode.rst:64
#: b1e6c82147154bfeae920532ad743b7f
msgid "QuadPlane wobbles on roll or pitch axis.  This usually means the Rate P values are incorrect.  See Copter Tuning section for some hints as to how to adjust the Q_A_xxx parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qstabilize-mode.rst:67
#: f6852798112d49f287dd5f7f0ecc8805
msgid "QuadPlane wobbles when descending quickly.  This is caused by the copter falling through its own prop wash and is nearly impossible to  tune out although raising the Rate Roll/Pitch P values may help."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qstabilize-mode.rst:70
#: 33be2aa143bd422ab2ecb2e21ee8db4f
msgid "QuadPlane yaws right or left 15degrees on take-off.  Some motors may not be straight or the escs need calibration :ref:`QuadPlane ESC Calibration <QuadPlane-esc-calibration>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qstabilize-mode.rst:72
#: e2989dd825de47fab39c4f5727f6998d
msgid "QuadPlane does not maintain altitude or does not stay perfectly still in the air.  As mentioned above this is a manual flight mode and requires constant control of the sticks to maintain altitude and position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qstabilize-mode.rst:76
#: 27d300d7381348cdb37466b7ee94e2a1
msgid "occasional twitches in roll or pitch.  Normally caused by some kind of interference on the receiver (for example FPV equipment placed too close to the receiver) or by ESC problems that may be resolved by :ref:`QuadPlane ESC Calibration <quadplane-esc-calibration>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qstabilize-mode.rst:80
#: 25c1bbf97b384d1c8146e128b95a0825
msgid "sudden flips during flight.  This is nearly always caused by :ref:`mechanical failures <copter:common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs_mechanical_failures>` of the motor or ESCs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qstabilize-mode.rst:85
#: ea455ce4a70d465fa993bfa23710b8ff
msgid "Hover Throttle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qstabilize-mode.rst:87
#: 6f36093c6aa543358933afc03738bc42
msgid "Usually, it is desired to hover in any mode at mid-stick on throttle, so that transitions between modes is easily accomplished without throttle position changes. This can be adjusted using the :ref:`Q_M_THST_HOVER<Q_M_THST_HOVER>` parameter, or automatically learned in QHOVER or QLOITER modes by enabling :ref:`Q_M_HOVER_LEARN<Q_M_HOVER_LEARN>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/qstabilize-mode.rst:89
#: 4672891896af4dc2b317f877c0964e8b
msgid "If :ref:`Q_THROTTLE_EXPO<Q_THROTTLE_EXPO>` = 0 in QACRO and QSTABILIZE modes, then :ref:`Q_M_THST_HOVER<Q_M_THST_HOVER>`, whether set manually or learned via :ref:`Q_M_HOVER_LEARN<Q_M_HOVER_LEARN>`, is not applied, and the throttle is determined directly from the RC input."
msgstr ""
